> "Leverage Points: Places to Intervene in a System" by Donella Meadows explores the concept of leverage points as strategic spots to influence and change complex systems. Meadows identifies different types of leverage points and ranks them by effectiveness, highlighting how small shifts in one part of a system can lead to significant changes in the whole. This work emphasizes the importance of understanding system dynamics to effectively address environmental and social challenges.
